  "pageshortdescription": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "shortDescTop": "<p><br>\r\nStryker’s 1688 AIM 4K Platform is the first system to 4K fluorescence! The entire tower is managed by the Connected OR Hub, giving you seamless connectivity to images, data, and settings you need. Now, surgical teams can see in greater detail than ever with superior image clarity, more accurate color reproduction, and enhanced light quality. With the added benefit of 4K fluorescence, the 1688 has truly taken visualization beyond the limits of any previous technology*</p>\r\n",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "lee.fuller1@stryker.com",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Aug 21 2020 16:34:32 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/pageshortdescription",
    "textIsRich": [
      "true",
      "true",
      "true"
    ]
  },
  "disclaimer": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "lee.fuller1@stryker.com",
    "disclaimer-type": "text",
    "disclaimer": "<p>References:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Jafari MD, Wexner SD, Martz JE, McLemore EC, Margolin DA, Sherwinter, DA, Lee SW, Senagore AJ, Phelan MJ, Stamos MJ. Perfusion Assessment in Laparoscopic Left Sided/Anterior Resection (PILLAR II): A Multi-Institutional Study. JACS. Vol. 220, No. 1, January 2015</li>\r\n<li>Data on file. Stryker Endoscopy. BZD14487. “Connected device management benchmark study”.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div>The 1688 Advanced Imaging Modalities (AIM) Platform includes the 1688 CCU and L11 Light source. SPY Fluorescence Technology includes SPY-PHI, the PINPOINT VPI, and PINPOINT camera. All uses of “AIM” herein refers to Advanced Imaging Modalities. AIM is not a trademark of Stryker Corporation.&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<div>*As compared to previous Stryker generation towers</div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n<p><i>**The SPY-PHI System is indicated for fluorescence imaging of blood flow and tissue perfusion before,&nbsp; during, and after: vascular, gastrointestinal, organ transplant, and plastic, microsurgical, and reconstructive surgical procedures. Upon interstitial administration of SPY AGENT™ GREEN, the SPY-PHI system is used to perform intraoperative fluorescence imaging and visualization of the lymphatic system, including lymphatic vessels and lymph nodes.</i></p>\r\n<p><i>The SPY-PHI system is indicated for use in adult cervical and uterine lymphatic mapping and pediatric patients one month of age and older.</i></p>\r\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Sep 04 2020 16:20:55 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/structure/disclaimer",
    "textIsRich": "true"
  },
  "contactbutton": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
